 ## Background
-Symmetric Matrix Stripping is used in 3D Gaussian Splatting and related rendering techniques to efficiently handle covariance matrices for Gaussian primitives [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It was popularized in implementations such as InstantSplat [S1, unofficial], FastGS [S2, unofficial], and 4D-Gaussian-Splatting [S3, unofficial] for optimizing the storage and processing of 3D Gaussians.
